# INOVAWAY Website — Coding Rules

## Stack
- Next.js 16.1.6 with App Router
- TypeScript (strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS v4
- Framer Motion for animations
- Shadcn/UI components
- next-intl v4 for i18n (PT-BR default, EN with /en/ prefix)
- Velite for MDX blog content
- Vercel deployment (auto-deploy via git push)

## Conventions
- Conventional commits: feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:
- Branch: master only (no feature branches unless asked)
- `npm run build` MUST pass before committing
- PT-BR is default locale (no URL prefix), EN gets /en/ prefix
- Never modify middleware.ts without explicit approval

## File Structure
- Components: src/components/
- Pages: src/app/[locale]/
- Blog content: content/blog/pt/ and content/blog/en/
- Public assets: public/
- Translations: messages/pt.json and messages/en.json

## Blog Posts
- MDX format via Velite
- Featured images: 1200x630px, no text in images
- Always bilingual (PT + EN), culturally adapted
- Brand terms never translated: AI Agents, INOVAWAY, UpBeez

## Quality
- No console.log in production code
- Proper TypeScript types (no any)
- Responsive design (mobile-first)
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, aria labels
